0,Melanau language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melanau_language,"Melanau is an Austronesian language spoken in the coastal area of the Rajang delta on northwest Borneo, Sarawak, Malaysia and Brunei. There are several dialects—Mukah-Oya, Balingian, Bruit, Dalat, Lawas, Igan, Sarikei, Segahan, Prehan, Segalang, and Siteng.","Melanau, Central",Austronesian
1,"Melanau, Central Language (MEL)... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mel/,"Central Melanau is an endangered indigenous language of Malaysia. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by a decreasing number of young people.","Melanau, Central",Austronesian
2,Western Austronesian,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Austronesian-Western.htm,"Click to: Western Austronesian-CN. Chamorro: Chamorro.Melanau: Central Melanau, Daro-Matu Melanau, Sibu Melanau, Melanau-Kanowit-Tanjong. Rejang-Sajau: Basap, Punan Bah Biau, Sajau Basap.","Melanau, Central",Austronesian
